Impeachment of the Chairperson and the Members of the Constitutional Tribunal of the Union
334. (a) The Chairperson and members of the Constitutional Tribunal of the Union may be impeached on any of the following reasons :
(i) high treason;
(ii) breach of any of the provisions under the Constitution;
(iii) misconduct;
(iv) disqualification of the qualifications of member of the Constitutional Tribunal of the Union prescribed under Section 333;
(v) inefficient discharge of duties assigned by law.
